 2. 🪿 What&#x27;s bad for the goose... 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Alex Fitzpatrick/Axios Share prices for luxury apparel maker Canada Goose are down amid tensions between the U.S. and longtime ally Canada, Axios' Emily Peck reports. 

 The company is known for its pricey parkas worn by various A-listers. 📉 Canada Goose stock has been falling all year amid higher tariffs from its southern neighbor.

 The prospect of a warmer winter courtesy of El Niño isn't great for the outerwear business either, Wells Fargo analysts noted this week. By the numbers: A 50% tariff on Canadian goods — which kicked in this past weekend — would increase Canada Goose's effective tariff rate on U.S. imports from 4.3% to 41.4%, per a Bank of America estimate.

