 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic: The Economist ; used with permission 🍔 The average American worker earns enough money to buy 10,215 Big Macs yearly, per The Economist's newly updated Big Mac index. It's a long-standing measurement of global purchasing power. Gift link . 💰 Meta agreed to settle with U.S. states for up to $16.7 billion in a landmark lawsuit over allegations that Facebook and Instagram were designed in ways that harm children. The company is calling on peers to sign on, saying the pact won't work unless they jointly line up behind broad reform. Meta agreed to limited under-18 users to two hours per day on Facebook and Instagram, block them from accessing the platforms from midnight to 6 a.m., and limit notifications during school hours. Go deeper . 🕯️ Actor Tim Curry, beloved for his outlandish and eccentric performances in "The Rocky Horror Picture Show," "Clue" and more, died yesterday at 80, his agent and manager said today. N.Y. Times obit . 🏀 The WNBA's Chicago Sky banned ex-NBA player Enes Kanter Freedom from Wintrust Arena following a verbal dispute with the Sky's Natasha Cloud. Kanter Freedom has been antagonistic toward transgender athletes, declaring to be a woman and claiming WNBA eligibility. Cloud is a vocal supporter of transgender people and other marginalized groups. Go deeper . A boy looks at the devastation caused by flash flooding along the Trishuli River in Nepal today. Photo: Niranjan Shrestha/AP Massive flash floods in a border area of Nepal and China killed at least 98 people and left hundreds missing. Get the latest . 

 
 
